WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:07.140
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
Publish turns Markdown into a site.

1
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.777
It will even read the page aloud,
highlighting the sentence as it goes.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.875
One sentence out of step is worse
than no highlighting at all.

3
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.560
And it points at the wrong line,
with total confidence.

4
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.280
13 tools carry a document from
Markdown to a page people can find.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.120
All 13 ship in the
package you install today.

6
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:48.440
A page with no Markdown behind
it is read exactly the same way.

7
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.650
Then the hard part. The audio
and the page leave by different roads.

8
00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.560
Sentences go to the voice engine.
Blocks are walked as a tree.

9
00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.760
So the module refuses to number
the sentences on its own side.

10
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.462
It takes the cues the narration wrote
and compares the two lists.

11
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:15.199
They match, or it refuses.
There is no third outcome.

12
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.525
This is the package's own documentation,
narrated and bound by it.

13
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.612
Watch the highlight.
The browser is doing that, not a script.

14
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.839
The cues are WebVTT,
the timed-text format of the web.

15
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:36.775
Not one line of synchronisation
code was written here.

16
00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:45.300
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:50.640
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
